═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
RSI ROADMAP: NEXT STEPS AND FUTURE IMPROVEMENTS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

PURPOSE: Document all next steps, pending improvements, and future
directions of the RSI (Recursive Self-Improvement) system.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
CURRENT STATE (2026-08-27)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

RSI Levels completed:
✓ Level 1: Auto-Optimization (rsi_metrics.py, rsi_feedback_loop.py)
✓ Level 2: Auto-Modification (rsi_gap_detector.py, rsi_tree_generator.py)
✓ Level 3: Auto-Generation (rsi_pattern_detector.py, rsi_predicate_generator.py)
✓ Level 4: Auto-Evolution (rsi_genetic_algorithm.py, rsi_forest_generator.py)

System components:
- 21 socratic trees (manual)
- 2 auto-generated trees (Level 2 & 3)
- 10 trees in forest (Level 4)
- 30 custom predicates
- 1 auto-generated predicate
- 6 logical operators
- 1 meta-tree (event_router)
- 1 pipeline tree (pipeline_classify)
- 1 memory tree (memory_classify)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
IMMEDIATE NEXT STEPS (1-2 weeks)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

1.1 GENETIC ALGORITHM TUNING
──────────────────────────────────────
Identified problems:
- Selection pressure too high → premature convergence
- Mutation rate too low → little exploration
- Fitness function too simple → needs more factors

Actions:
- Reduce tournament size (3 → 2)
- Increase mutation rate (0.1 → 0.2)
- Add factors to fitness (diversity, complexity, etc.)
- Maintain population diversity

1.2 FITNESS FUNCTION IMPROVEMENT
──────────────────────────────────────
Current factors:
- Accuracy (40%)
- Complexity (20%)
- Branch diversity (20%)
- Threshold range (20%)

Factors to add:
- Latency (penalize slow trees)
- Coverage (reward trees covering more cases)
- Stability (reward consistent trees)
- Novelty (reward new vs existing trees)

1.3 DIVERSITY MAINTENANCE
──────────────────────────────────────
Mechanisms to implement:
- Limited elitism (keep only top 10%)
- Duplicate penalty
- Genetic diversity reward
- Niches (different tree types)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
SHORT-TERM IMPROVEMENTS (1 month)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

2.1 ENGINE EXTENSIONS (Proposals for socratic-engine)
──────────────────────────────────────
Proposed extensions:
- MAP (iteration over lists)
- FOLD (reduction)
- FILTER (filtering)
- MEMO (cache results)
- RECURS (recursion with guard)

Benefit:
- Would enable runtime modification
- Would enable real crossover
- Would enable real mutation
- Would make the system more powerful

Required action:
- Propose to socratic-engine
- Implement if there is demand
- Improve Level 4 with extensions

2.2 REAL CROSSOVER (Subtree exchange)
──────────────────────────────────────
Current implementation:
- Crossover by gene mixing
- Not real subtree exchange

Improvement:
- Identify cut points in trees
- Exchange subtrees between parents
- Maintain syntactic validity
- Requires engine extensions

2.3 REAL MUTATION (Branch modification)
──────────────────────────────────────
Current implementation:
- Mutation by value changes
- Not real structure modification

Improvement:
- Add/remove branches
- Modify conditions
- Change actions
- Requires engine extensions

