LONG-TERM IMPROVEMENTS (6+ months)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

4.1 CO-EVOLUTION (Predator-Prey)
──────────────────────────────────────
Concept:
- Classifier trees vs adversarial trees
- Joint evolution of both
- Dynamic equilibrium

Implementation:
- Classifier population
- Adversary population
- Cross-evaluation
- Joint evolution

4.2 SPECIATION (Different tree types)
──────────────────────────────────────
Concept:
- Different tree species
- Each species specialized
- Independent evolution
- Species composition

Implementation:
- Define species (fast, accurate, etc.)
- Separate evolution per species
- Composition for specific tasks
- Solution diversity

4.3 SIMULATED ECOSYSTEM
──────────────────────────────────────
Concept:
- Multiple interacting populations
- Limited resources
- Competition and cooperation
- Ecosystem evolution

Implementation:
- Define resources (data, computation)
- Competing populations
- Cooperation when beneficial
- Complete ecosystem evolution

